<title>UK: UK business failures drop to seven-year low.</title>
<headline>UK business failures drop to seven-year low.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of business failures in the UK has dropped to its lowest level in seven years, the Times said on Monday.</p>
<p>Citing figures from Dun and Bradstreet, the paper said failures during the first six months of the year fell to under 20,000, the first time that had happened since the beginning of the recession.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
